      "text": [
        " : كُنَّا جَمِيعاً فَاشْتَرَيْنَا طَيْراً فَقَصَصْنَاهُ فَدَخَلْنَا بِهِ مَكَّةَ فَعَابَ ذَلِكَ أَهْلُ مَكَّةَ فَأَرْسَلَ كَرِبٌ إِلَى أَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ فَسَأَلَهُ فَقَالَ «اِسْتَوْدِعُوهُ رَجُلاً مِنْ أَهْلِ مَكَّةَ ، مُسْلِماً أَوِ اِمْرَأَةً مُسْلِمَةً فَإِذَا اِسْتَوَى خَلَّوْا سَبِيلَهُ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2362 - Al-Muthanna narrated from Karib al-Sayrafi:\nWe were a group who collectively purchased a bird, clipped its feathers, and entered Makkah with it. The people of Makkah disapproved of this action. Karib sent someone to Abu Abdullah (as) to inquire about it.\nImam (as) said: \"Entrust it to a Muslim man or woman from the people of Makkah, and when its feathers grow back, release it.\""
        ]
      }
